## Purpose

Materialize gate and accepted-risk states as a post-gate, non-authority review projection without modifying the semantic `mxGraphModel` that was checked.

```text
semantic mxGraphModel
  -> geometry facts + findings
  -> policy + exact waiver gate
  -> dispositions + verification/decision/risk
  -> generated overlay
  -> review.drawio + receipts
```

## Accepted architecture

ADRS Decision `01KYE5TYW0TQNMVHFTRZT3R2SF` is Accepted at `doc://adrs/post-gate-decision-overlay-v1` through roccho-dev/adrs#258, merge `aaf7024366d1877b60f04c4207b48da096a86ab0`.

The accepted boundary remains:

- ADRS owns accepted meaning;
- `diagrams/events.jsonl` remains diagram-event authority;
- semantic model, gate report, receipts, and review view remain generated non-authority outputs;
- no second current-state schema is introduced.

## Added

- axis-aligned rectangle relation inspection using the Python standard library;
- parent-containment, partial-overlap, route-coverage, and unrelated edge-obstacle findings;
- independent `verification`, `gateStatus`, `decision`, and `risk` axes;
- exact, time-bounded waivers bound to finding, subject, and policy digests;
- fail-closed stale, expired, future-issued, over-duration, mismatched, and unknown waivers;
- generated draw.io XML user objects on a dedicated overlay layer;
- semantic/review artifact discrimination and review-input rejection;
- one `materialize-review` CLI entry;
- geometry, gate, projection, and Nix receipts;
- deterministic rebuild and fixed-editor proof workflows;
- locked Nix input and declared Nix test dependency.

## Artifact contract

```text
diagram.semantic.drawio
  checker/roundtrip input

diagram.geometry.json
  observed facts/findings + coverage
diagram.gate.json
  dispositions + verification/gateStatus/decision/risk
diagram.gate-receipt.json
  semantic/policy/waiver/report digests
diagram.review.drawio
  semantic base + generated non-authority overlay
diagram.projection-receipt.json
  base/gate/projector/output digests
```

A review artifact is rejected when either its user-object metadata declares `artifactKind=diagram.review.v1` or a `role=decision-overlay` object exists. V1 intentionally does not strip overlays to recover semantic input.

## Waiver invariant

A valid waiver may change:

```text
disposition: open -> accepted
decision: DENY -> ALLOW
risk: OPEN -> ACCEPTED
```

It may not change facts, findings, verification coverage, semantic geometry, or semantic identity. Diagram text such as `ACCEPTED` has no waiver authority.

## Exact merge proof

Current head: `3c75d0166cf82a8fb7b3bfb25d2e383fae3a18d1`.

All current merge-ref workflows are green:

- Post-gate decision overlay proof: run `30188230640`;
- Diagram artifact gallery: run `30188230648`;
- Work View proof: run `30188230657`.

The post-gate run proves on the current merge ref:

- dedicated post-gate and user-object tests pass;
- the full canonical test suite passes;
- accepted-risk materialization is `ALLOW / ACCEPTED / PARTIAL`;
- repeated materialization is byte-identical;
- fixed draw.io Desktop `30.0.4` performs actual UI edit and save;
- semantic user objects, stable IDs, review marker, overlay metadata, and overlay-layer ownership persist;
- saved review artifacts remain rejected from semantic entries;
- competing overlay/current-state files and DVM/RenderAst dependencies are absent from the new modules;
- `nix flake check -L` passes;
- `nix build -L .#jsonl-diagram-core` passes.

Retained artifacts:

- post-gate/editor proof: `8627696063`, `sha256:b9e53400d8e5a67a7ffe2d5192d2e530ead0af6b441bcf4233ae361c01959f93`;
- Nix proof: `8627691019`, `sha256:1cd9683f2dca1b390de08da0a24ff77ba36f37a5609200936aa093c1520ce144`.

The workflow checks out GitHub's PR merge ref, so the proof includes the current `proposals` base commits as well as this head. The PR remains mergeable and has zero unresolved review threads.

## Claim ceiling

This PR does not claim:

- DVM deletion or #6 closure;
- approval-reference signature authenticity;
- correctness of COO/CPO responsibility or purpose-contribution claims;
- render-exact text, rotation, z-order, opacity, font, theme, or dark-mode inspection;
- exact connector routing when only source/target centers are known;
- all-repository enforcement;
- business outcome or corporate-sale achievement.

Center-to-center routes explicitly retain `verification=PARTIAL`.

## Rollback

Rollback may remove the overlay projector, review artifact, and projection receipt while retaining the semantic diagram, geometry facts/findings, policy/waiver evidence, accepted ADRS meaning, and event authority.

## Merge gate

- [x] parent ADRS decision Accepted and read back;
- [x] full canonical tests pass on the current merge ref;
- [x] deterministic replay passes;
- [x] fixed draw.io UI edit-save persistence passes;
- [x] saved review artifacts remain rejected;
- [x] Nix flake check and canonical package build pass;
- [x] accepted risk cannot appear as clean success;
- [x] zero unresolved review threads;
- [x] PR is ready for review and mergeable.

Merge with expected-head protection. After merge, read back the implementation from `proposals` and keep DVM cutover under #6 separate.

