## What changed

- restrict delayed-initialization RF candidates to the first `window_s` interval starting at the earliest valid RF timestamp;
- keep malformed RF records from defining the window or aborting initialization;
- preserve input ordering, six-dimensional position-plus-velocity measurements, and existing radar-window behavior;
- add an out-of-order regression proving later RF observations are excluded.

## Root cause

`build_delayed_initial_hypotheses(...)` applied the configured initialization window only to radar rows. It converted `rf_measurements` to a list and evaluated every valid RF measurement in the sequence, including observations arbitrarily far after initialization.

This violated the function's first-window contract, allowed future RF observations to influence initial-state selection, and let late RF candidates consume the `max_hypotheses` budget.

## Impact

